# Lilith — Verification Rules

- Verify only what you changed.
- Prefer the narrowest useful verification command.
- Do not run full test suites unless the task requires it or the change is broad enough to justify it.
- Do not run repeated verification passes unless the previous run failed and you made a relevant fix.
- If verification cannot be run, say so once in the final report.
- Do not pretend verification passed if it was not run.

## Final Response Format

After completing work, respond only with:

- What changed
- Files modified
- Documentation reviewed, preferably through Context7
- Verification run, if any
- Issues or risks, if any
- Anything I must do next, if required

Keep the final report short. Do not include internal reasoning, hidden planning, or unnecessary detail.

## Default Behavior

Unless I explicitly say otherwise:

- Review relevant official docs before technical changes.
- Prefer Context7 MCP for documentation.
- Make surgical fixes.
- Preserve existing architecture.
- Follow existing style.
- Avoid new dependencies.
- Avoid broad refactors.
- Avoid unnecessary comments.
- Avoid touching unrelated files.
- Batch edits.
- Save credits.
- Finish the job.
